Fix scheduled GDMS run's BST drift and status-dropdown GDMS gap (v0.134)

Dan tested the scheduled GDMS run and found it fired at 17:30 instead of
16:30, then found a cancelled test order's device still showing assigned
in GDMS.

1. GdmsEndOfDayService.scheduledRun()'s cron had no timezone, so it ran
   on the container's UTC clock - 16:30 UTC is 17:30 in the UK while BST
   is in effect, which is exactly what Dan saw. Pinned to Europe/London
   so it's 16:30 UK time all year.

2. There are two ways to cancel an order in this app, and only one of
   them touched GDMS: the dedicated "Cancel & Return to Stock" button
   does a full recall+stock+carton unwind via GdmsRecallService, but
   picking "Cancelled" from the order's own Status dropdown
   (OrderService.update()) was a bare status flip with no GDMS call at
   all. Added the same recall call there too, scoped to just the GDMS
   side (that dropdown path still doesn't touch stock/cartons, which is
   a different, deliberate behaviour from the dedicated button).

Separately investigated why Dan's device stayed assigned even though he
confirmed he used the correct "Cancel & Return to Stock" button, not the
dropdown - that code path is correct and does call GDMS's own
/channel/recycle endpoint as documented, but per this project's own GDMS
findings doc, that endpoint had never actually been exercised against
the real GDMS account before today, only confirmed against GDMS's
documented shapes. No code changes for this part - the GDMS Sync Log
(Admin > GDMS Log) records the real success/failure and error message
per attempt, which is the next place to check.

